\f1\b\fs40 NextEvent\
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
NextEvent puts a countdown to your next calendar event or reminder in the menu bar, so you always know how much time you have before your next meeting.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
{{\NeXTGraphic Image1.png \width8000 \height7140 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
}¬}
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\
\f1\b\fs32 Getting Started
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\'95	Open NextEvent. Its icon appears in the menu bar at the top right of your screen.\
\'95	When macOS asks, allow NextEvent to access your calendars and reminders.\
\'95	Click the icon, choose Preferences, and check the calendars and reminder lists you want to follow.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\
\f1\b\fs32 Seeing Your Events
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
Click the NextEvent icon in the menu bar to see what\'92s coming up. For each event you\'92ll see:\
\
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\'95	A box on the left with the time until it starts, such as \'933 HOURS\'94. The colored strip across the top matches the event\'92s calendar.\
\'95	The event\'92s title.\
\'95	Its date and time, and how long until it starts.\
\'95	Its location, if it has one.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
Events that have already started are grayed out.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Click an event
\f0\b0  \'97 Calendar opens on the day of that event. The first time, macOS asks whether NextEvent can control Calendar. Click Allow.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Click a reminder
\f0\b0  \'97 The reminder opens in Reminders.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Bottom of the menu
\f0\b0  \'97 Open Calendar or Reminders, Refresh the list, open Preferences or this Help, or Quit NextEvent.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Right-click the icon
\f0\b0  \'97 A shorter menu with Refresh, About, Preferences and Quit.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\
\f1\b\fs32 Preferences
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
Click the menu bar icon and choose Preferences.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
{{\NeXTGraphic image2.png \width5000 \height10820 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
}¬}
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b\fs28 Alerts
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Flash at 15 minute mark
\f0\b0  \'97 The menu bar icon flashes during the last 15 minutes before an event.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Flash blue
\f0\b0  \'97 The icon flashes blue instead of orange.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Use System Alert
\f0\b0  \'97 Shows a standard macOS notification when an event starts.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Use Blocking Alert
\f0\b0  \'97 Covers your screen with an alert you have to dismiss, so you can\'92t miss an event.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Early Warning
\f0\b0  \'97 Available when Blocking Alert is on. Shows the blocking alert 1, 3 or 5 minutes before the event instead of when it starts. Choose 0 to show it right at the start.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Use Travel Time
\f0\b0  \'97 If an event has travel time set in Calendar, NextEvent alerts you and flashes the icon when it\'92s time to leave.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Play chime
\f0\b0  \'97 Plays a sound with alerts.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b\fs28 Menu Bar
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Use alternate icon
\f0\b0  \'97 Uses the Mazookie \'93M\'94 icon instead of the calendar icon.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Show Time on menu bar
\f0\b0  \'97 Shows the countdown next to the icon, as days:hours:minutes. For example, 0:02:15 means 2 hours 15 minutes.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Use fuzzy time
\f0\b0  \'97 Shows a rounded time instead, such as \'935 minutes\'94 or \'93tomorrow\'94.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Show Title on menu bar
\f0\b0  \'97 Shows the next event\'92s title next to the icon.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Use Title Limit
\f0\b0  \'97 Shortens titles longer than 20 characters so they don\'92t crowd the menu bar.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Show seconds
\f0\b0  \'97 Adds seconds to the countdowns in the menu bar and the menu.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Show leading zeros
\f0\b0  \'97 Shows every unit in the menu\'92s time remaining, such as \'930 days 2 hours 5 minutes\'94 instead of \'932 hours 5 minutes\'94.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b\fs28 Which Events to Show
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Number of events
\f0\b0  \'97 Choose how many upcoming events to list:\
\
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\'95	1, 3, 5 or 10 \'97 that many upcoming events.\
\'95	Today only \'97 all of today\'92s events, including ones that have already happened.\
\'95	24 Hours \'97 everything in the next 24 hours.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Calendars & Reminders
\f0\b0  \'97 Check the calendars and reminder lists to include. If none are checked, no events are shown.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\
\f1\b\fs32 Troubleshooting
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b The menu shows N/A
\f0\b0  \'97 There are no upcoming events in the calendars you\'92ve checked. Make sure at least one calendar or reminder list is checked in Preferences.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b No events appear at all
\f0\b0  \'97 Go to System Settings > Privacy & Security > Calendars (and Reminders) and make sure NextEvent is allowed.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Clicking an event doesn\'92t go to it
\f0\b0  \'97 Go to System Settings > Privacy & Security > Automation and turn on Calendar under NextEvent.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-720\partightenfactor0
\f1\b Something looks out of date
\f0\b0  \'97 Choose Refresh from the menu.\
\
